From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:23:40 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: apple: macaudio, arm64: dts: t6040-j614s: Keep the
 J614s speakers off

The J614s ships experimental and its speakers need their own bring-up.
There is no J614 protection profile and the speakers have not been
measured, so nothing may drive them.

Give the J614 speaker card its own configuration with the speakers
disabled, so the driver never binds the speaker link even if the card
is enabled. In the J614s device tree disable the speaker card and the
six SN012776 amps as well, so no amp driver probes and no stream can
reach them. The headphone jack card is unchanged. The J616s keeps its
configuration and its DTB is unchanged.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(cherry picked from commit 7915d686b4560fe54cdfaefbe9f995f7febafcb8)
[dylan: Dropped the t6040-j614s.dts hunk because omacom has no J614s
 device tree. The macaudio.c j614 speakers-off configuration is taken
 unchanged. The J604 device tree follows the same convention later in
 this series.]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c b/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
index 545ee2ab0e..1a7519c2ea 100644
--- a/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
+++ b/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
@@ -2143,6 +2143,27 @@ struct macaudio_platform_cfg macaudio_j616_cfg = {
 	.route_only_fes = BIT(0),
 };
 
+/*
+ * J614s: the same amps and frame as the J616s, but its speakers have not
+ * been brought up and have no protection profile. Keep them off entirely
+ * until they get their own bring-up: the speaker link is not bound, so no
+ * stream ever reaches the amps.
+ */
+struct macaudio_platform_cfg macaudio_j614_cfg = {
+	.enable_speakers = false,
+	.amp = AMP_SN012776,
+	.speakers = SPKR_2W1T,
+	.stereo = true,
+	.amp_gain = 15,
+	.safe_vol = -20,
+	.fe_dai_names = { "j616-pcm-0", "j616-pcm-1", "j616-pcm-2" },
+	.dai_fmt = SND_SOC_DAIFMT_I2S | SND_SOC_DAIFMT_CBC_CFC |
+		   SND_SOC_DAIFMT_GATED | SND_SOC_DAIFMT_NB_IF,
+	.secondary_bclk_ratio = 250,
+	.fe_cpu_is_platform = true,
+	.route_only_fes = BIT(0),
+};
+
 /*
  * The J614s and J616s headphone jack, a card of its own: a CS42L84 on the
  * AOP's "jack" back-end, which the firmware runs on MCA cluster 2 as a 64-SCLK
@@ -2226,8 +2247,8 @@ static const struct of_device_id macaudio_snd_device_id[]  = {
 	/* j575    AID33   sn012776    15      1x 1W    Compat: apple,j375-macaudio */
 	/* j613    AID20   sn012776    15      2x 1W+1T Compat: apple,j413-macaudio */
 	/* j615    AID21   sn012776    15      2x 2W+1T Compat: apple,j415-macaudio */
-	/* j614    AID34   sn012776    15      2x 2W+1T (AOP-fed, one serializer) */
-	{ .compatible = "apple,j614-macaudio", .data = &macaudio_j616_cfg },
+	/* j614    AID34   sn012776    15      2x 2W+1T (AOP-fed; speakers off until bring-up) */
+	{ .compatible = "apple,j614-macaudio", .data = &macaudio_j614_cfg },
 	/* j614    AID34   cs42l84     -       the jack, a card of its own (AOP-fed) */
 	{ .compatible = "apple,j614-macaudio-jack", .data = &macaudio_j616_jack_cfg },
 	/* j616    AID35   sn012776    15      2x 2W+1T (AOP-fed, one serializer) */
